 is extremely important to  language learning in other words i  believe i can get better i believe that  every day that i put effort in whether  it's an hour or three hours reading  listening speaking  however much i stumble however much i  struggle  i know that it is contributing towards  my improvement i'm convinced of it i'm  an optimist  i ge i have given myself a 90-day period  in which to make a significant  improvement i will make that significant  improvement i'm quite convinced i'm an  optimist and i think  optimism is important to language  learning  i think optimism is important to life i  get very annoyed  when i read these sort of negative  comments about today that you know we're  ruining the planet  politicians are all corrupt it's not  worthwhile voting  uh capitalism consumerism is destroying  the world i mean  it that is just absolute absolute  nonsense  by any standard  we are so much better off today than at  any time before in history  life expectancy was 30 half or more of  children who were born died  if there was a poor harvest some year  because it was cold or rained too much  people had nothing to eat  nowadays  we can eat  produce from  california spain  indonesia it doesn't matter and then  there are people who complain we should  only eat the local produce what a bunch  of nonsense again if therefore if you're  in sweden all you get to eat is potatoes  and herring you shouldn't have citrus  fruit because it's not local  of course we're better off to be able to  access food from all over the world and  those countries that export their  produce they're better off because  they're able to export it it's a  wonderful world uh we have seven and a  half billion people on the planet for  the longest time we had the same you  know a few hundred million so  of course it has an impact on  certain ecosystems but that doesn't mean  the world is being destroyed it means  that  there's been a growth in the human  population which has perhaps caused  